  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "Passive energy recovery; transformation unlocks repeated area damage and battle stat growth.",
    "skill1": "Dash through all enemies, dealing damage and stun while invincible.",
    "skill2": "Gain a temporary shield and unaffected status, then recover HP from its remainder.",
    "skill3": "Permanently increase ATK after assists or defeats.",
    "skill4": "Inflict HP-loss with an execute against a lone weakened enemy.",
    "skill5": "Temporarily increase allied ATK behind the caster and grant a named ally Energy."
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Taichi & Agumon]] keeps the human partner off-field while the companion gains Energy and prepares the first transformation. After transforming, the duo combines repeated area damage with an invincible path through the enemy team. A large temporary shield provides an Unaffected recovery window before converting into healing. The execute gives strong finishing pressure when only one weak enemy remains, while the team-facing ATK bonus rewards allies positioned behind the transformed fighter. Early control or burst before the first ultimate delays the transformation and removes much of the kit.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Taichi & Agumon]] is weakest before the first ultimate transforms the pair; afterward, invincible charges, an Unaffected shield window, and an execute make repeated control unreliable. Deny or delay that transformation with [[Dunlingr]]'s ultimate lockout, then pressure the duo early with [[filter:backline-assassin]] like [[Ravion]] or [[Himmel]]. Do not dump CC into the invincible path or shield window, and keep a durable second target alive so the execute cannot close the fight. Race the first ultimate with [[filter:energy-provider]] like [[Thador]] or [[Hugin]]."
}
